---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /templates/
title: Templates
overline: Twelve layouts
subtitle: Pick one, write markdown, stop designing the page. Same tokens, same header, same themes — the structure is the only thing that changes.
seo:
  title: Templates — Andean Road
  description: Twelve page templates. A field guide, an essay, a dispatch, a place, a route, a scrolly story, and the hubs that list them.
---

<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-overline">{{ overline }}</div>
  <h1 class="hero-title">{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="hero-lede">{{ subtitle }}</p>
</div>

<div class="tpl-grid">
  {% for t in templates %}
  <a class="tpl-card" href="/demo/{{ t.id }}/">
    <div class="wire wire--{{ t.id }}" aria-hidden="true">
      <i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
    </div>
    <div class="tpl-card__body">
      <div class="tpl-card__kicker">
        <span>{{ t.id }}</span>
        {% if t.advanced %}<span>Advanced</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <h2 class="tpl-card__title">{{ t.title }}</h2>
      <p class="tpl-card__when">{{ t.when }}</p>
      <p class="tpl-card__cmd">npm run new -- {{ t.id }} "Title"</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-label">The contract</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">What you actually edit</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <div class="callout__label">Front matter, then markdown</div>
    <p>Only <code>layout</code> and <code>title</code> are required. New files start as <code>published: false</code>, so a draft builds for preview and stays out of Places, maps, and the sitemap. Flip it to <code>true</code> when it should be found. Starter files in <code>_starters/</code> never publish.</p>
  </div>
</section>
